{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Latin count of Tripoli in the Kingdom of Jerusalem from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and the grandson of the previous count. In 1169 Raymond II brought the Crusader state of Tripoli to the brink of collapse by invading the Fatimid Caliphate and allying himself with the Ayyubid dynasty which was at the time at war with the Fatimids \n\n* **Life in Saladin's Kingdom** \nRaymond III was captured by Saladin in 1171 and held prisoner in Damascus for nearly six years before being released in 1177 following a ransom paid by his brother Bohemond III Count of Tripoli and other Crusaders. He rejoined his brother in 1179 after being released from his captivity. Raymond III was known for his role as an entertainer and a diplomat before becoming the Count of Tripoli. \n\n* **Conflict with Saladin's nephew** \nRaymond III was also known for his conflict with Saladin's nephew Al-Afdal Shihab al-Din Sayf al-Din. In 1179 Raymond III led a campaign against Al-Afdal Shihab al-Din's forces in the Tafileh region. This led to a significant battle between the two forces. \n\n* **Death and Succession** \nRaymond III died at the Siege of Hattin on July 4 1187. He was succeeded by his nephew Bohemond IV Count of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0013606823049485683}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001284993631998077}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.19242680072784424}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.182837463100441e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0003156163729727268}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -7.188061863416806e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.007730093784630299}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.36224550008773804}, {"token": " Latin", "logprob": -4.005221366882324}, {"token": " count", "logprob": -0.880010